# {{.product_name}}

Gold-layer data product, deployed as a Databricks Asset Bundle with Azure DevOps CI/CD.

## Targets

| Target    | Mode        | Catalog        | Schema                 | Deployed by         |
| --------- | ----------- | -------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------- |
| `dev`     | development  | `{{.catalog}}` | `{{.schema}}_dev`      | you (interactively) |
| `staging` | production   | `{{.catalog}}` | `{{.schema}}_staging`  | staging SP (CI)     |
| `prod`    | production   | `{{.catalog}}` | `{{.schema}}`          | prod SP (CI)        |

## Develop

```bash
databricks bundle validate -t dev
databricks bundle deploy   -t dev
databricks bundle run {{.product_name}}_build -t dev
```

Put pure logic in `src/transformations.py` and keep `src/build_gold.py` thin (it
just wires widgets to Spark). Add more jobs, pipelines, or dashboards under
`resources/`.

## Test

Unit tests for the pure logic in `src/transformations.py` run with **no cluster**:

```bash
pip install -r tests/requirements.txt
pytest
```

The pipeline runs these on every PR (the `validate` stage). The Spark job itself
is exercised end-to-end by the integration test —
`databricks bundle run {{.product_name}}_build -t staging` — in the staging stage.

## Ship

Open a PR to `main` (the pipeline validates it), merge (deploys to staging and runs
an integration test), then a platform approver promotes it to prod.
